1
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,810
Emilia-sama and Natsuki Subaru-sama,

2
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:11,610
I would gladly host you two at 
my home for as long as you need.

3
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,670
We appreciate that,

4
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:17,690
but we do want to get the 
villagers back home.

5
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:19,600
We'll come back after we take them all home

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,500
and talk to her sponsor, Roswaal.

7
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,290
Very well.

8
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:28,290
When you do, I hope I can finally 
repay my great debt to you.

9
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:32,290
It's not that big a deal. 
You helped us out, too.

10
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:35,590
We even got a reward. Right, Patrasche?

11
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:38,160
Ow!

12
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,350
Are you all right, Subaru?

13
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:41,880
Those scales hurt more than I expected!

14
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:44,750
Now I know how a daikon radish 
feels when it's being grated!

15
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:50,200
Subaru-kyun, I've secured Rem-chan.

16
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,950
Be sure to keep her still!

17
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:53,940
Okay.

18
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:58,590
You'll need your rest when you 
get back to the mansion, too.

19
00:00:58,590 --> 00:00:59,350
Me?

20
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:03,370
You've been working your gate overtime 
since you were going up against Sloth.

21
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,920
I did clean up all the toxins in your gate,

22
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:09,040
but you need to let it rest for two months.

23
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:10,780
Two months, huh?

24
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:14,570
Well, surely all this crazy stuff 
can't keep happening for <i>that</i> long...

25
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,930
Wait, did I just set a flag?!

26
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:20,830
All right, it's time for you to get going.

27
00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:22,240
Go on, Crusch-sama.

28
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,170
Give them a few parting words.

29
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:28,640
Emilia-sama, I wish you good health.

30
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:32,070
I look forward to seeing you again very soon.

31
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,820
You, too, Crusch-san. Please be well.

32
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:43,680
Next time, I won't just be the 
one who always needs saving.

33
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:46,370
I'll become someone who can help others.

34
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,600
Natsuki Subaru-sama,

35
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,670
I wish you all the best in the future, too.

36
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,980
I know we will meet again.

37
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,620
Right, then...

38
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:31,890
You know, Subaru, you always sit beside 
me as if it's the obvious choice.

39
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:33,920
Oh, is there something weird about that?

40
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,420
No. I felt a little uncomfortable at first,

41
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:40,890
but now it feels strange if 
you don't, so it's fine.

42
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:45,330
My painstaking efforts have 
finally been rewarded!

43
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:46,580
I'm so moved!

44
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,230
You're teasing me again.

45
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:51,860
I know you're still worried about Rem.

46
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:54,980
There's no need for you to hide that.

47
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,050
She's important to you, isn't she?

48
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:00,680
She is! Super important!

49
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,570
As important to me as you are!

50
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,080
You're being very selfish.

51
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:06,910
Are you aware of that?

52
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:08,810
Sure, I am.

53
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:11,040
Frankly, I feel like such scum,
 I wish I could die.

54
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:13,670
But it's the absolute truth.

55
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:15,840
Subaru...

56
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:20,530
Did you just say my name?

57
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,230
No, I didn't!

58
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:24,990
Wait, have you been there all this time?

59
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:27,320
Of course I've been here!

60
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:30,680
Why do you think I decided 
to work with you?!

61
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:32,300
I'm just kidding.

62
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,300
You want to negotiate with Roswaal in person.

63
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:36,460
I haven't forgotten that.

64
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:40,400
I'm begging you! My whole 
life is riding on this!

65
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,440
Yeah, yeah, I got it.

66
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:45,780
Time to say goodbye to you for now.

67
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,780
Oh, wai—

68
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:57,460
I'm sure you'll find a way to get her back.

69
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:00,170
Emilia-tan...

70
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:04,590
Also, I think you and I
 are the same in the sense

71
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,890
that we act for our own selfish reasons.

72
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:13,270
I realize that I'm participating in the 
royal selection for selfish reasons, too.

73
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:14,850
Selfish?

74
00:04:15,470 --> 00:04:18,980
I'm sorry... I can't explain it very well.

75
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,400
I don't want to hide anything from you,

76
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,570
but I'm not sure how to put it into words.

77
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:32,930
We can talk everything out 
after we join up with Roswaal.

78
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:37,250
He might know something about 
what happened to Rem, too!

79
00:04:38,770 --> 00:04:39,440
Right.

80
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:45,060
You two, we'll be reaching 
our destination soon!

81
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,140
No one's here.

82
00:04:53,290 --> 00:04:55,030
No one around here, either.

83
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:57,500
What? Why?

84
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:00,760
So Ram and the others haven't 
returned from the Sanctuary?

85
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,240
Seems that way.

86
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:06,050
By the way, Emilia-tan, do you 
know where the Sanctuary is?

87
00:05:06,050 --> 00:05:09,280
Huh? I thought <i>you</i> knew where it was.

88
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:09,910
Huh?

89
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:14,100
I know I'm late in asking,

90
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:16,580
but what kind of place is 
the Sanctuary, anyway?

91
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:18,490
I'm not sure, either.

92
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:22,670
Roswaal only said it was like 
a secret base... and...

93
00:05:22,670 --> 00:05:23,540
And?

94
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,130
Nothing, never mind.

95
00:05:26,570 --> 00:05:29,140
I'm sorry. I should have asked.

96
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:31,950
No, no! Even if we were in 
a hurry to get to safety,

97
00:05:31,950 --> 00:05:34,400
I'm the one who was way too careless!

98
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:40,950
We'll just have to head to the mansion for now.

99
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,610
Maybe we'll find some clues there.

100
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:44,860
Otto, come with us!

101
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:47,240
What? To the mansion?

102
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:49,850
Don't be so scared after 
we've come this far.

103
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,670
Take the carriage and the ground 
dragons around back, okay?

104
00:05:52,670 --> 00:05:54,500
All right...

105
00:05:59,410 --> 00:06:01,460
We're back, Rem.

106
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:03,440
Are you all right?

107
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:04,420
Yeah.

108
00:06:04,730 --> 00:06:08,300
Come to think of it, I don't remember 
locking the door when we left.

109
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,550
You think we got robbed?

110
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:13,850
Beatrice stayed here, so I 
don't think we need to worry.

111
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:16,680
Maybe she'll come get the 
door for us if we knock.

112
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,960
She might come flying through 
it, looking for Puck.

113
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:21,690
That's true.

114
00:06:22,580 --> 00:06:24,610
Puck? Puck?

115
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:27,600
Huh? He's not responding.

116
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,320
Maybe he's asleep.

117
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,360
How about in here?

118
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,570
Yes, one moment, please.

119
00:06:38,590 --> 00:06:41,550
Welcome home, Emilia-sama.

120
00:06:41,550 --> 00:06:44,500
I have awaited your return.

121
00:06:45,170 --> 00:06:46,210
Frederica?

122
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:51,360
Yes, it is I, Frederi—

123
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,430
Those teeth are scary!

124
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,750
Allow me to introduce myself.

125
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:59,810
I am Frederica Baumann. I was 
employed here in the past.

126
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:02,620
Now that you mention it,

127
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:05,690
I was told there was another maid 
who quit just before I came here...

128
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:10,010
I merely took my leave for personal reasons.

129
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:14,910
Then I returned at Ram's request, 
and found the mansion empty.

130
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:18,520
Fortunately, a letter I found 
in the master's office

131
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:20,710
gave me an idea as to what had happened.

132
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:21,600
A letter?

133
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,170
And why did Ram ask you to come back?

134
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:26,490
When I returned,

135
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,560
the kitchen and the trees in the 
garden were in a desolate state.

136
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,010
It was quite awful.

137
00:07:33,330 --> 00:07:34,970
That's a pretty serious reason!

138
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:38,270
It's strange, though.

139
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:42,750
Ram has always worked hard 
for us while you were away,

140
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:44,690
so why, in just the past few days...

141
00:07:47,670 --> 00:07:50,940
With Rem gone, Ram couldn't 
handle the mansion herself,

142
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,660
so she asked Frederica to help?

143
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:58,370
Would you mind explaining 
to me who this girl

144
00:07:58,370 --> 00:07:59,870
who bears a striking resemblance to Ram is?

145
00:08:00,450 --> 00:08:02,530
She's Ram's younger sister, Rem.

146
00:08:02,530 --> 00:08:04,350
She's a really nice girl.

147
00:08:04,930 --> 00:08:08,180
She's kind, strong, and a super-hard worker.

148
00:08:08,570 --> 00:08:12,930
Even I could tell that she 
and Ram were really close.

149
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:16,580
I'm sure you were a good friend to her, too.

150
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:21,350
You... probably don't remember, though, right?

151
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:23,910
Unfortunately, no.

152
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:28,070
I wonder how the master and Ram 
will react when they return...

153
00:08:28,530 --> 00:08:30,660
I can't even guess what Roswaal will do.

154
00:08:31,310 --> 00:08:34,280
And... I don't want to 
imagine how Ram will react.

155
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:39,630
Hey, Frederica, have you 
heard anything from Roswaal?

156
00:08:39,630 --> 00:08:44,790
Sadly, I have no way of knowing all 
that goes on in the master's mind.

157
00:08:45,430 --> 00:08:51,260
I believe there are only two people in 
this world he trusts enough for that.

158
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:52,800
Two?

159
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:56,680
Ram and the great spirit of this 
mansion's forbidden library.

160
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:58,720
Great spirit of the forbidden library?

161
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,110
I refer to Beatrice-sama.

162
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:15,700
Hey, Beako! Long time no see!

163
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:20,460
Now I see why the mansion 
suddenly seemed so noisy.

164
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:25,410
Everyone's been worried about you.

165
00:09:25,410 --> 00:09:27,790
You should apologize, even if 
it has to wait until later.

166
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:30,670
Apologize? Me?

167
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:34,170
I fail to comprehend why I 
must apologize, and to whom, I suppose.

168
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:37,260
I could go apologize for you, if you want.

169
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:40,930
I'll tell them you were thanking me with 
tears and snot streaming down your face.

170
00:09:40,930 --> 00:09:42,810
Don't make up stories!

171
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,600
I haven't shed tears in a 
very long time, I suppose.

172
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:48,250
It never hurts to have a good 
wail every once in a while.

173
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:50,320
Those words carry deep meaning,

174
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:53,780
coming from a man who bawled in 
the lap of the woman he loves.

175
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:56,550
Would you just forget about that already?

176
00:09:56,550 --> 00:09:58,800
Could you please get to the point, I suppose?

177
00:09:58,800 --> 00:09:59,950
You weakling.

178
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,180
Oh, yeah...

179
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:07,080
How well do you know what 
Roswaal's thinking?

180
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:13,800
Someone told me that you 
know how Roswaal thinks.

181
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:15,520
Who said—

182
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:16,270
Ah.

183
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,590
It must have been the 
half-beast girl who just came back.

184
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:24,280
There is a bit of accuracy to 
what she told you, I suppose.

185
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:28,730
But my connection with Roswaal has nothing 
to do with the current circumstances.

186
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:31,800
But you stayed here at the mansion by yourself,

187
00:10:32,190 --> 00:10:34,070
even with no countermeasures in place.

188
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:36,990
I'm capable of protecting myself.

189
00:10:36,990 --> 00:10:39,160
That's why I stayed, I suppose.

190
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:41,600
Roswaal has nothing to do with that.

191
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:46,080
That said, I don't believe he had 
nothing on his mind at all, I suppose.

192
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,490
Hmm...

193
00:10:47,490 --> 00:10:53,300
Were you and I and everyone else 
just giving him too much credit,

194
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:56,230
thinking he wouldn't go up against 
the Witch's Cult with no plan?

195
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:58,460
Oh, that's right.

196
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:00,860
Take a look at this.

197
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:04,760
A Gospel...

198
00:11:05,350 --> 00:11:08,600
Why do you, of all people, 
have one of those?!

199
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:11,220
I took it off the enemy after a battle.

200
00:11:11,220 --> 00:11:14,980
It belonged to the guy in charge of the witch 
cultists who surrounded the mansion.

201
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,690
And what became of him?

202
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:19,110
He's dead.

203
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:21,280
I killed him.

204
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,930
Then you've left me behind, too, I suppose...

205
00:11:28,070 --> 00:11:29,160
Geuse.

206
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,120
Who's that?

207
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,850
None of your concern.

208
00:11:34,350 --> 00:11:38,800
Anyway, if you killed Sloth, a Sin Archbishop,

209
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,630
what happened to his Witch Factor?

210
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:43,140
Witch... Factor?

211
00:11:43,750 --> 00:11:46,510
You don't know what it is? You really don't?

212
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:51,160
If that's the case, then why 
did you bother to kill Sloth?

213
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:53,150
And what is Roswaal...

214
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:56,930
I told you, remember? 
Roswaal is at the Sanctuary!

215
00:11:56,930 --> 00:11:59,580
I'm the one who wants to 
know what he's thinking!

216
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:06,120
All the answers you seek lie 
in the Sanctuary, I suppose.

217
00:12:06,690 --> 00:12:07,640
What?

218
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:10,930
Roswaal's intentions, the meaning of the Gospel,

219
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:14,120
answers about the Witch Factor...
They're all there.

220
00:12:14,970 --> 00:12:16,670
If you want them, go there.

221
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:20,760
The half-beast girl can 
lead you there, I suppose.

222
00:12:21,030 --> 00:12:23,410
Hang on a second! What's up with you?

223
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:25,320
Why are you suddenly willing to talk to me?

224
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,480
Also, why do I have to go to 
the Sanctuary when you—

225
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,070
I will not tell you.

226
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:32,770
I have the right to refuse to tell you.

227
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:37,040
I showed you the path that 
leads to your answers.

228
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,560
Do not expect me to indulge 
you any further, I suppose!

229
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,560
Beako... Beatrice!

230
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:45,200
I am not a tool here for your convenience!

231
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:54,120
Wh-Why did you fly into me just 
as I was leaving the bathroom?!

232
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:57,210
Why did you look like you 
were about to cry again?

233
00:12:57,210 --> 00:12:59,090
Excuse me! Could you please get off of—

234
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:05,130
So you really are allowed to enter 
Beatrice-sama's forbidden library?

235
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,510
What? You thought I wouldn't be?

236
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:12,810
Yes, but Emilia-sama has told me 
what a reliable person you are,

237
00:13:12,810 --> 00:13:15,510
and she was quite thorough 
in explaining why,

238
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:18,560
so half of me had high
hopes that you would be.

239
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:18,980
Huh?

240
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:20,720
Hey! Frederica!

241
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:22,480
What? What did you tell her?

242
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:27,740
It's not like that! I did tell her 
about you, but she's exaggerating!

243
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:30,680
No, I heard what you said, too.

244
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:33,370
It made me think there must be more 
to Natsuki-san than meets the eye.

245
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:34,900
Not you, too, Otto-kun!

246
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:38,540
Why wasn't I around to hear all this?!

247
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,420
I could never say it in front of you.

248
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:43,870
Now, Frederica, back to what you were saying!

249
00:13:43,870 --> 00:13:46,090
Yes, of course. I know.

250
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:50,830
Let us talk it over so you don't 
find yourself at a dead end.

251
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,840
Dead end? What do you mean?

252
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,880
Even if you were able to see Beatrice,

253
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:58,030
whether or not she'd answer your 
question was another matter.

254
00:13:58,030 --> 00:14:01,730
Both you and Beatrice can be 
very stubborn, you know.

255
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:05,960
That description is way too cute,
 but you're right.

256
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:06,700
And?

257
00:14:07,210 --> 00:14:10,460
There's a lot I want to talk 
to Roswaal about, too.

258
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,700
So I asked Frederica

259
00:14:13,130 --> 00:14:15,010
to tell me where the Sanctuary is.

260
00:14:16,270 --> 00:14:19,540
The half-beast girl can 
lead you there, I suppose.

261
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:23,060
So you're going to tell us 
where it is, Frederica?

262
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:25,770
I was no match for 
Emilia-sama's persistence,

263
00:14:25,770 --> 00:14:29,620
even though I have been told not to 
disclose any more than necessary.

264
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,220
But I would like to ask 
for a bit of time to prepare.

265
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:35,390
Shall we say two days?

266
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,970
Prepare?

267
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:41,350
Oh, that's right. We'd all be 
leaving the mansion, so that's—

268
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:44,280
No, I will be staying in the mansion.

269
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,440
I cannot accompany you.

270
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,800
What? You're not going with us?

271
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,540
How are we supposed to get there, then?

272
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,390
You're rather slow on the uptake, Natsuki-san.

273
00:14:56,600 --> 00:15:00,530
Oh! So Otto's gonna get us to the Sanctuary?

274
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:03,430
Because he thinks cooperating 
with Emilia in any way possible

275
00:15:03,430 --> 00:15:07,710
will give Roswaal, her backer, 
a better impression of him?

276
00:15:05,530 --> 00:15:07,050
No, er...

277
00:15:07,710 --> 00:15:09,510
Otto-kun, is that true?

278
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,840
Emilia-sama's pure, innocent 
eyes are killing me!

279
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,800
I'm sorry! That's exactly right!

280
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:18,670
The way you wear your ulterior motive on your
 sleeve makes you all the more likable, Otto.

281
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:21,480
That's not exactly comforting, 
coming from you!

282
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:23,290
I appreciate your help.

283
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:27,040
On that note, you can tell the 
three of us about the Sanctuary.

284
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,190
Very well.

285
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,430
What I am about to tell you

286
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:36,280
is the undisclosed location of the Sanctuary 
of Clemaldy, and how to enter it.

287
00:15:36,990 --> 00:15:42,080
And there is one name you must 
not forget as you travel there.

288
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:45,500
Beware of one by the name of "Garfiel."

289
00:15:46,020 --> 00:15:47,250
At the Sanctuary,

290
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:53,420
he will be the one with whom you 
must exercise the most care.

291
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:00,980
Rem...

292
00:16:01,670 --> 00:16:02,880
We're leaving now.

293
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:06,920
I told Frederica to take good care of you.

294
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:08,780
Be good and wait here for me, okay?

295
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,120
You're ready?

296
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,450
Sure am, new recruit.

297
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:23,760
I see you're rocking the uniform already.

298
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:24,940
Right?

299
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:29,940
Did you say goodbye to Rem-san?

300
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:31,820
Yeah, something like that.

301
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,510
We're not planning to stay out there long,

302
00:16:34,510 --> 00:16:35,890
but I wanted to see her first.

303
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:41,470
Could you take care of Rem for 
me while I'm gone, Petra?

304
00:16:42,130 --> 00:16:44,310
Understood, Subaru-sama!

305
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:48,110
Still, we started advertising to 
hire a new maid two days ago,

306
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:50,430
and this is your first day 
actually being in the mansion.

307
00:16:50,430 --> 00:16:52,900
I'm impressed you found the 
place without getting lost.

308
00:16:53,370 --> 00:16:57,160
And I really admire your decision to 
leave your parents at such a young age.

309
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:00,630
I'm twelve years old! I'm old 
enough to be a working grown-up!

310
00:17:00,630 --> 00:17:02,290
I mean... an adult!

311
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:06,240
You need to treat me like 
an adult, too, Subaru-sama!

312
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:09,770
Get better at speaking politely and 
get Frederica to fully initiate you,

313
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:10,900
and I'll think about it.

314
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:11,640
'Kay!

315
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:12,880
I mean... yes, sir!

316
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:21,910
I forgot what a pain she can be 
when she's serious about hiding.

317
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:24,890
Is there really a mysterious room here?

318
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:27,060
Yeah... Beatrice.

319
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,700
You know her, right? 
Take care of her for me, too.

320
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:35,280
You might randomly encounter her 
when opening a door somewhere.

321
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,870
Wait, Subaru-sama! Aren't you 
asking a bit much of me?

322
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,910
I know. Sorry.

323
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:43,320
But you're the only one I can ask.

324
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:44,580
I really am sorry.

325
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,440
Oh, all right!

326
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:52,090
If you insist, I'll just have to help you out!

327
00:17:52,090 --> 00:17:54,010
Thanks. You're really a huge help.

328
00:17:55,430 --> 00:17:57,560
Take care of the mansion for us.

329
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:00,220
And Rem, Petra, and Beatrice, too.

330
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,360
You can rely on me.

331
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:05,180
Take care during your travels, Emilia-sama.

332
00:18:05,990 --> 00:18:07,550
And take this.

333
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:10,720
This will allow you to get past 
the barrier in the forest,

334
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,940
and enter the Sanctuary.

335
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:17,780
From there, the ground dragons should 
take you to the location I described.

336
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:22,060
So this stone is the requirement 
to get through the barrier?

337
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,790
You have the location and the qualification.

338
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:31,110
Now you only need the 
resolve and a strong will.

339
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,830
Frederica...

340
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,820
Take good care of the Sanctuary.

341
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,680
And do not forget what I said earlier.

342
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:45,870
Okay. We'll watch out for Garfiel.

343
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,110
I promise.

344
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,880
Um, Subaru-sama...

345
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:53,320
Would you please accept this?

346
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,230
Uh...

347
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,140
Lending a white handkerchief to a traveler,

348
00:18:57,140 --> 00:19:00,280
who later returns it stained 
and worn from the journey,

349
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:03,870
is an old custom performed as 
a prayer for safe travels.

350
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:06,260
Oh, it's one of those things?

351
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,060
Okay, got it. Thanks, Petra.

352
00:19:09,490 --> 00:19:10,670
I promise I'll return it.

353
00:19:17,830 --> 00:19:20,580
What? What brought that reaction on?

354
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:23,640
This sudden rebellious phase is making me sad.

355
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,760
Now, you should hurry.

356
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:32,850
The Lost Forest of Clemaldy grows 
more dangerous as night approaches.

357
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,260
I wish you a safe journey.

358
00:19:39,390 --> 00:19:41,490
Subaru-sama!

359
00:19:42,170 --> 00:19:45,770
You'd better protect the lady!

360
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:50,090
I have done exactly as Master directed.

361
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:56,630
Now everything depends on how 
Emilia-sama overcomes the Sanctuary.

362
00:19:57,110 --> 00:19:59,120
There is nothing we can do but pray.

363
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:03,840
Puck isn't showing up?

364
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:05,350
Yeah.

365
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:07,040
I've called out to him several times,

366
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:09,430
and I can feel the link 
from our contract, but...

367
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:12,180
Has anything like this happened before?

368
00:20:12,180 --> 00:20:15,760
Not very often, but there 
have been a few times

369
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:18,150
when he didn't show up for a few days.

370
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:23,530
I'm counting on you to take care of Lia.

371
00:20:24,130 --> 00:20:25,140
Couldn't have been...

372
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:29,560
But I do have contracts 
with lesser spirits, too,

373
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,690
and I can also fight with them.

374
00:20:31,690 --> 00:20:34,410
No matter what happens, I'll protect you!

375
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:36,360
Wow, you're so manly!

376
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,360
Hey!

377
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:43,340
Frederica did warn us that 
something might happen.

378
00:20:43,340 --> 00:20:45,940
Oh... Garfiel, right?

379
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:50,520
Yeah. Roswaal did mention a few times 
that he was going to see him...

380
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:51,720
Excuse me!

381
00:20:52,010 --> 00:20:53,620
We're in the forest!

382
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:59,650
<i>The Lost Woods of Clemaldy.</i>

383
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:03,660
A special barrier there protects the Sanctuary.

384
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:07,410
It makes outsiders lose their way, 
to prevent them from getting close.

385
00:21:07,910 --> 00:21:11,120
That is why they call it the "Lost Woods."

386
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:14,190
So the Sanctuary is just ahead...

387
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:23,780
Emilia-tan, are you actually nervous?

388
00:21:23,780 --> 00:21:25,930
Huh? How could you tell?

389
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:28,700
I know everything about you!

390
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:32,160
At least, that's what I'd like 
to say, but anyone could tell.

391
00:21:36,550 --> 00:21:37,940
You're right!

392
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:41,260
I'm sorry for worrying you.

393
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,490
When I think that we're about 
to arrive at the Sanctuary,

394
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:45,900
a village where only demihumans live...

395
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:50,330
No, I should apologize. I wasn't 
thinking that far ahead.

396
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:54,910
I guess there might be more 
half-elves like you there, huh?

397
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:59,390
I've never seen any half-elves 
other than myself.

398
00:21:59,990 --> 00:22:02,630
But just maybe, in the Sanctuary...

399
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:05,970
Don't worry. I'll—

400
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:08,970
Emilia?!

401
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,970
Uh... Is this...

402
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:13,320
I suddenly have a really bad feeling!

403
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:14,430
I'm borrowing this, Emilia!

404
00:22:18,810 --> 00:22:19,860
Emilia!

405
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:33,990
Where... am I?

406
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,150
Who are you?

407
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:46,690
Those ears...

408
00:22:46,690 --> 00:22:48,130
Are you an elf?

409
00:22:49,300 --> 00:22:51,910
No, wait! Wait a minute!

410
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:05,050
Hey! Is anyone here?

411
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:09,090
If this is the Sanctuary, 
somebody answer me!

412
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:14,570
This is...

413
00:23:29,390 --> 00:23:30,340
I see.

414
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:33,880
So that is the root of your desire?

415
00:23:33,880 --> 00:23:36,170
How very interesting.

416
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:48,600
Oh, did I startle you?

417
00:23:52,230 --> 00:23:55,430
It has been quite a while 
since I spoke with anyone,

418
00:23:55,430 --> 00:23:57,690
so perhaps I was too eager.

419
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,080
My name is Echidna...

420
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:06,310
Or perhaps you would know me 
better as the Witch of Greed?

421
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,960
The Next Location

422
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:19,960


423
00:25:18,410 --> 00:25:18,910
If it's

424
00:25:20,450 --> 00:25:20,950
to save you

425
00:25:21,740 --> 00:25:22,160
I don't care

426
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:23,660
how many times

427
00:25:25,540 --> 00:25:26,330
I die

